IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch7-p4`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch7-p4.l4 (Schedule 7 Parts IV and V). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 7 Parts IV and V`

§§ `Paragraph 11(1) -- entitlement`

-- Argument order: employed earner; (a) pension entitlement; (b)(i); (b)(ii); (b) alternative (incapable since the 90 days);
-- accident on or after 1 Oct 1990 (extent); disease prescribed on or after 10 Oct 1994; extension of an earlier prescription (extent).
-- A pre-1990 accident, (a) and both limbs of (b): entitled.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The alternative limb of (b) alone is enough.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only (b)(i), not (b)(ii), and not the alternative: not entitled.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an employed earner; no pension entitlement.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Loss of faculty wholly from an accident on or after 1 Oct 1990: no. Partly: the text apportions nothing, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV wholly` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV partly` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A disease prescribed on or after 10 Oct 1994: no. An extension of an earlier prescription: wholly no; partly NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` TRUE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV wholly` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `sch 7 pt IV not at all` FALSE `sch 7 pt IV partly` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 11(2), (3)`

-- Argument order: entitled immediately before 1 Oct 1990; subsequently ceased for a day or more; the day last entitled; the day the new period commences.
-- Last entitled 31 Dec 1991: a period commencing 1 Jan 1992 (the next day) is not prevented (NOTHING); 2 Jan 1992 is barred (FALSE).
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(2) the person may again be entitled for the period` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 1991) (Date 1 1 1992) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(2) the person may again be entitled for the period` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 1991) (Date 2 1 1992) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(2) the person may again be entitled for the period` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 12 1991) (Date 15 6 1991) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not entitled before 1 Oct 1990, or never ceased: the bar does not arise.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(2) the person may again be entitled for the period` FALSE TRUE (Date 31 12 1991) (Date 2 1 1992) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(2) the person may again be entitled for the period` TRUE FALSE (Date 31 12 1991) (Date 2 1 1992) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(3)(a) the person is treated as entitled on the day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(3)(a) the person is treated as entitled on the day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(3)(a) the person is treated as entitled on the day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 11(5), (6)`

#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5)(a) the occupation counts as the regular occupation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5)(a) the occupation counts as the regular occupation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5)(a) the occupation counts as the regular occupation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5)(b) the employment may count as employment of an equivalent standard` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5)(b) the employment may count as employment of an equivalent standard` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5) regard is to be had to the reasonable prospect of advancement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(5) regard is to be had to the reasonable prospect of advancement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(6) the person is treated as incapable of following the regular occupation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(6) the person is treated as incapable of following the regular occupation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 11(8) to (14) -- period, rate and limits`

#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(8)(b) the allowance may be awarded for a further period` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(8)(b) the allowance may be awarded for a further period` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 11(9): assessed period 1 Jan to 31 Dec 2025 (365 days); an award of the same length (even if shifted) is not caught; 366 days is.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(9) the award may be for the period` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(9) the award may be for the period` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 2 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(9) the award may be for the period` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(9) the award may be for the period` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Maximum rate: pass-through (Schedule 4 omitted).
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(14) the maximum rate of a disablement pension` (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(14) the maximum rate of a disablement pension` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 11(12A): any of the three.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12A) the person is a person who retired from regular employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12A) the person is a person who retired from regular employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12A) the person is a person who retired from regular employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12A) the person is a person who retired from regular employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- 11(10)/(11): maximum 200, disablement pension 100. Caps: 40% = 80; 140% - 100 = 180 over 200*1.4=280-100=180. Lesser is 80.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 200) 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST 80
-- Disablement pension 230: 280 - 230 = 50 is lesser than 80 -> 50.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 200) 230 FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
-- A person who retired before 6 April 1987: 100% -> 200 - 230 < 0 -> 0; with pension 150: 50.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 200) 230 TRUE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 200) 150 TRUE EQUALS JUST 50
-- Exactly equal caps: pension 200 gives 280 - 200 = 80, equal to 40% -> 80.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 200) 200 FALSE EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` NOTHING 100 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rate: the judged rate or the cap, whichever is lesser; unknown inputs give NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 60) (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 90) (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the rate of reduced earnings allowance` NOTHING (JUST 80) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST 60) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 11(12): regulations under (4) -> the accident occupation; otherwise the regular occupation.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12) the relevant occupation` TRUE "miner" "foreman" EQUALS "miner"
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12) the relevant occupation` FALSE "miner" "foreman" EQUALS "foreman"

§§ `Paragraph 12 -- supplementary`

-- 12(1): on 10 April 1988 or 9 April 1989 with all three conditions -> JUST TRUE; any other day, or a condition missing -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 10 4 1988) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 9 4 1989) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 11 4 1988) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 10 4 1988) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 10 4 1988) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(1) the person is entitled to reduced earnings allowance for life` (Date 10 4 1988) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 12(5), (6): the relevant date.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(5) the relevant date` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 4 1988)
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(5) the relevant date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 4 1988)
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(5) the relevant date` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 9 4 1989)
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(5) the relevant date` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 12(4): entitled under (1); (a) or (b); restricted rate. One of (a)/(b) suffices.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(4) the person is a qualifying beneficiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(4) the person is a qualifying beneficiary` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(4) the person is a qualifying beneficiary` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(4) the person is a qualifying beneficiary` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(4) the person is a qualifying beneficiary` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- 12(2), (3): qualifying beneficiary on 10 April 1988 -> 25.84; 9 April 1989 -> 26.96; another date -> NOTHING; not qualifying -> the supplied rate.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(2) the weekly rate of the allowance for life` TRUE (Date 10 4 1988) (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 25.84
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(2) the weekly rate of the allowance for life` TRUE (Date 9 4 1989) (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 26.96
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(2) the weekly rate of the allowance for life` TRUE (Date 1 1 1990) (JUST 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(2) the weekly rate of the allowance for life` FALSE (Date 10 4 1988) (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(2) the weekly rate of the allowance for life` FALSE (Date 10 4 1988) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(7) the person is a person who has retired from regular employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt IV para 12(7) the person is a person who has retired from regular employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 13 -- retirement allowance`

-- 13(1): gives up on or after 10 April 1989 (the day itself counts); the day before (9 April) does not.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(1) the day from which the person ceases to be entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE (Date 10 4 1989) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 4 1989)
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(1) the day from which the person ceases to be entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE (Date 9 4 1989) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(1) the day from which the person ceases to be entitled to reduced earnings allowance` FALSE (Date 10 4 1990) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(1) the day from which the person ceases to be entitled to reduced earnings allowance` TRUE (Date 10 4 1990) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 13(2): £2.00 threshold: 1.99 -> FALSE; 2.00 -> TRUE; not ceasing -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) the person is entitled to retirement allowance` TRUE 1.99 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) the person is entitled to retirement allowance` TRUE 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) the person is entitled to retirement allowance` TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) the person is entitled to retirement allowance` FALSE 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) what the benefit is called` EQUALS `retirement allowance`
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(3) retirement allowance may be payable on the day` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(3) retirement allowance may be payable on the day` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 13(5): the £26.96 assumption applies only to both limbs together.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(5) the weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance taken for sub-paragraph (4)` TRUE TRUE 30 EQUALS 26.96
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(5) the weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance taken for sub-paragraph (4)` TRUE FALSE 30 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(5) the weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance taken for sub-paragraph (4)` FALSE TRUE 30 EQUALS 30
-- 13(4): 25% of 40 = 10; 10% of the maximum 200 = 20 -> lesser 10. 25% of 100 = 25 against 20 -> 20. Equal: 25% of 80 = 20 -> 20.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(4) the weekly rate of retirement allowance before rounding` 40 (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(4) the weekly rate of retirement allowance before rounding` 100 (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(4) the weekly rate of retirement allowance before rounding` 80 (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(4) the weekly rate of retirement allowance before rounding` 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 13(6): 10.00 stays; 10.014 pounds = 1001.4 pence, fraction .4 -> NOTHING (the text does not round it); 10.015 = 1001.5 pence -> 10.02; 10.019 -> 10.02.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` 10 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` 10.014 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` 10.015 EQUALS JUST 10.02
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` 10.019 EQUALS JUST 10.02
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` 10.02 EQUALS JUST 10.02
-- 13(10): either limb true; both false; unknown.
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(10) the day is a day of interruption of employment` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(10) the day is a day of interruption of employment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(10) the day is a day of interruption of employment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(10) the day is a day of interruption of employment` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(10) the day is a day of interruption of employment` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 7 pt V para 13(11) the maximum rate of a disablement pension` (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 200
